{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:76fbe6787718be60","name":"Ysalamiri","source":{"id":"source:reference-76fbe6787718be60","title":"Ysalamiri","revision":19060,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:13:46Z","sha256":"c017c75d2c9b6cafe4bbf3e805a8b51a88be7f65fd266d40cdd2c813684eae6b","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19060","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Ysalamiri&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-76fbe6787718be60","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Ysalamiri are tiny creatures native to the planet ",{"tag":"a","children":["Myrkr"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Myrkr?action=edit&redlink=1"},". They grow to be up to half a meter long, are covered in fur, and superficially resemble snakes with legs. The typical Ysalamiri spends most of its life in a motionless state, attached by its claws to the metal-rich trees that form its primary habitat. The creatures are difficult to remove from the trees once they have attached themselves, and they will die 1d4 days after being removed.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The most interesting aspect of the Ysalamiri is its ability to push back or repel ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," in a spherical area centered on itself. It has been hypothesized that this ability evolved as a defense mechanism against the Ysalamiri's primary predator on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Myrkr"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Myrkr?action=edit&redlink=1"},", the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vornskr"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vornskr","referenceId":"reference:f5bdbc4aecca503f"},". Since ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vornskrs"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vornskrs"}," depends on Force powers in order to locate and bring down prey, the Ysalamiri's ability to push back ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," makes the small creatures much harder for these predators to locate.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Ysalamiri Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Despite their ability to nullify ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},", Ysalamiri are largely peaceful and inoffensive. They remain immobile for most of their lives, and are largely incapable of physically defending themselves from predators. If attacked, Ysalamiri remain motionless, as they are anchored to a tree.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Ysalamiri are occasionally sought out by individuals who wish to use them as shields against Force powers. This tactic was first employed by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Grand Admiral Thrawn"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Grand_Admiral_Thrawn"}," in his assault on ",{"tag":"a","children":["The New Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_New_Republic","referenceId":"reference:e6046dbb57e5abb0"},". It is possible that Ysalamiri might be utilized in this fashion to foil the powers of Jedi and other Force-users. Prior to this time, Ysalamiri were largely unknown throughout the galaxy, so it is quite unlikely they would be encountered in the earlier eras.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Ysalamiri Statistics (CL 0)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Tiny ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," 1\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," -2; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a"